# The game's pieces, in glue order. build.py joins them into starship-cadet.html; split.py cuts that file back into them.
# Order is part of the game (load order, and the R() sequence): never move a line without a full check run.
# Each line: PIECE  PICK  BACK  MARKER
#   MARKER: a regular expression for one line of the game file; the piece starts BACK lines before that line
#           (1 = at the ==== banner above a "// 19. DEVICE" title; -1 = the line after the marker).
#   PICK:   once = the marker must be found exactly once; first / last = take the first / last of several.
# The first piece has no marker (it starts the file). A section heading named here is load-bearing: rename it here too.
page/head.html
page/css.css                     once   -1  ^<style>$
page/body.html                   once    0  ^</style>$
js/s01-setup-materials.js        first  -1  ^\(\(\) => \{$
